# Task 5 — Pseudocoding evidence repository
#
# No environment variables are required for this repository.
#
# This repository contains only Markdown evidence documents (pseudocode,
# hand traces, comparisons, and notes). It does not run any application
# code and connects to no services, so there is nothing to configure.
#
# This file exists so the repository has a clear, safe template and so that
# a real `.env` file is never needed or committed. Do not add credentials,
# tokens, passwords, API keys, or real environment values here.
#
# If the referenced Medlink-ai project ever needs environment variables,
# document them in that project's own `.env.example`, not in this evidence
# repository.
